# MrWhoOidc request samples (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client).
#
# Values target the seeded `docker-compose.dev.yml` stack:
# - Protocol endpoints are tenant-prefixed; the seeded issuer is https://localhost:8443/t/default
#   (see docs/developer-guide.md section 1; read exact URLs from the discovery document).
# - `blazor-web` is a confidential, PKCE-required client (authorization_code, refresh_token,
#   token-exchange and client_credentials grants). Its dev secret is the
#   `DEV_SEED_BLAZOR_WEB_CLIENT_SECRET` value in `.env` — the same value the RazorClient demo uses.
# - The stack serves a self-signed development certificate: trust it with
#   `dotnet dev-certs https --trust`, or configure your client to skip verification for local testing only.

@issuer = https://localhost:8443/t/default
@client_id = blazor-web
@client_secret = your-dev-seed-blazor-web-secret
@redirect_uri = https://localhost:5003/Auth/Callback

### Discovery
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### JWKS (server signing keys; cache with ETag)
GET {{issuer}}/jwks

### Client JWKS (optional; requires Auth:ExposeClientJwks, on in the dev stack)
GET {{issuer}}/clients/{{client_id}}/jwks

### Authorize (manual browser step)
# Open in a browser and sign in (dev stack: admin@mrwho.local and SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD from .env).
# {{issuer}}/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{client_id}}&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&scope=openid%20profile%20email%20offline_access&code_challenge={{code_challenge}}&code_challenge_method=S256&state=xyz&nonce=abc

### Pushed Authorization Request (PAR; returns a single-use request_uri)
POST {{issuer}}/par
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

response_type=code&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&scope=openid%20profile&code_challenge={{code_challenge}}&code_challenge_method=S256&state=xyz&nonce=abc

### Token: exchange authorization code (PKCE + client_secret_post)
POST {{issuer}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code={{code}}&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&code_verifier={{code_verifier}}&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}

### Token: refresh grant
POST {{issuer}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{refresh_token}}&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}

### Token: client credentials
# blazor-web also has the client_credentials grant. When you pass `resource`,
# it must be in `Auth:ApiAudiences` or the client's `M2MAllowedAudiencesJson`.
POST {{issuer}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}

### UserInfo
GET {{issuer}}/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Introspection (confidential clients only: own, aud-named, or granted tokens)
POST {{issuer}}/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token={{access_token}}&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}

### Revoke refresh token
POST {{issuer}}/revoke
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token={{refresh_token}}&token_type_hint=refresh_token&client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}

### End session (RP-initiated logout; manual browser step)
# post_logout_redirect_uri must be a registered post-logout URI for the client.
# {{issuer}}/connect/endsession?id_token_hint={{id_token}}&post_logout_redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5003%2F&state=logout

### Device authorization (requires Auth:EnableDeviceAuthorizationGrant=true
# and a client with AllowDeviceAuthorization)
POST {{issuer}}/device/authorize
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client_id}}&client_secret={{client_secret}}&scope=openid

### Token exchange (OBO): see obo-token-exchange.http
